---
const rules = [
  {
    title: 'Complete against a named rival',
    body: 'Every app covers everything its benchmark does. The parity table in its roadmap is the scoreboard.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Fixed once, below the interface',
    body: 'A shared substrate owns storage, sync and credentials, so a bug is fixed in one place and every app stays a thin front end.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Nothing siloed',
    body: 'Panel applets, launcher plugins, daemons, portals and shared settings. The apps talk to the desktop and to each other.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Wayland and the GPU, no apologies',
    body: 'Layer-shell surfaces where they fit, and wgpu as the one rendering path that gets tuned.',
  },
];
---

<section class="brief" aria-labelledby="brief-title">
  <p class="label">How it’s made</p>
  <h2 id="brief-title" class="section-title">The brief every app is built against</h2>

  <ul class="rules">
    {rules.map((rule) => (
      <li>
        <h3>{rule.title}</h3>
        <p>{rule.body}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <div class="measured">
    <p class="label">Measured in September 2026</p>
    <p class="log">
      <span><b>~200,000</b> lines of Rust</span>
      <span><b>2,268</b> tests</span>
      <span><b>0</b> <code>todo!()</code> calls</span>
      <span>Apps <b>GPL‑3.0</b>, substrate <b>MPL‑2.0</b></span>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .brief {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem) var(--gutter);
    background: rgb(4 6 12 / 0.88);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .rules {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem 2.5rem;
    max-width: 72rem;
  }

  .rules li {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--field);
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-stretch: 125%;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .rules p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .measured {
    margin-top: 4.5rem;
    max-width: 72rem;
  }

  .log {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.6rem 2.5rem;
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-stretch: 85%;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }

  .log b {
    color: var(--corona);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .log code {
    color: var(--corona);
  }
</style>
